==English==
[[Image:Clenched human fist.png|thumb|right|A clenched [[fist]].]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|clenchen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|clenċan|t=to clinch; hold fast}}, a variant of {{inh|en|ang|clenġan|t=to adhere; remain}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*klangijaną}}, [[causative]] of {{m|gem-pro|*klinganą|t=to stick; adhere}}. Related to {{m|en|cling}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/klɛnt͡ʃ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-clench.wav|Audio (UK)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛntʃ|s=1}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}} {{tlb|en|ambitransitive}}

# To [[grip]] or hold fast.
#* {{RQ:Dryden Aeneis}}
#*: '''Clinch''' the pointed spear.
# To close tightly.
#: {{ux|en|He '''clenched''' his fist in anger.}}
#* {{RQ:Tennyson Idylls|page=179|passage=[She] flung herself / Down on the great King's couch, and writhed upon it, / And '''clench'd''' her fingers till they bit the palm, / And shriek'd out 'traitor' to the unhearing wall, {{...}}}}

